IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ppl-logic`
IMPORT `ppl-time`
IMPORT `ppl-nouns`

-- Paid Parental Leave Act 2010 (Commonwealth), compilation C2026C00425, Chapter 2 Part 2-3 Division 3 (sections 32 to 36AA): the work test.
-- The days of the work test period are supplied as a list, earliest day first, one record for each day (see ppl-nouns).
-- What is paid work, paid leave, an employee's control of an entity, a jobkeeper payment and the hours taken for a payment period
-- depends on the PPL rules, which are not among the sources; those are asked as inputs.

-- src:762 | (2A) This subsection applies in relation to a PPL claimant or special PPL claimant if:
-- src:763 | (a) the PPL claimant or special PPL claimant is pregnant with the child or is the birth mother of the child; and
-- src:764 | (b) the PPL claimant or special PPL claimant is performing or performed paid work of a particular kind before the birth of the child; and
-- src:765 | (c) the PPL claimant or special PPL claimant will cease or ceased performing that kind of work on a particular day (the claimant’s work cessation day) because of hazards connected with that kind of work that pose or posed a risk to the pregnancy; and
-- src:766 | (d) any conditions prescribed by the PPL rules are satisfied.
@ref s 33(2A) (src:762-766)
GIVEN `the claimant is pregnant with the child or is the birth mother of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is performing or performed paid work of a particular kind before the birth of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant will cease or ceased performing that kind of work because of hazards connected with it that pose or posed a risk to the pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any conditions prescribed by the PPL rules are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`subsection 33(2A) applies in relation to a claimant` MEANS
    JUST (        `the claimant is pregnant with the child or is the birth mother of the child`
          AND `the claimant is performing or performed paid work of a particular kind before the birth of the child`
          AND `the claimant will cease or ceased performing that kind of work because of hazards connected with it that pose or posed a risk to the pregnancy`
          AND `any conditions prescribed by the PPL rules are satisfied`)

-- src:742 | (1A) This section applies in relation to a PPL claimant or special PPL claimant who is not a COVID-19 affected claimant in relation to a claim for parental leave pay for a child.
@ref s 33(1A) (src:742-742)
GIVEN `the claimant is a COVID-19 affected claimant in relation to the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 33 applies to a claimant` MEANS
    IF `the claimant is a COVID-19 affected claimant in relation to the claim` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:743 | (1B) If a provision of this Act or the PPL rules requires a person (the first person) to satisfy the work test on a day for the purposes of a PPL claim or special PPL claim made by another person, this section applies as if a reference to a PPL claimant or special PPL claimant were a reference to the first person.
@ref s 33(1B) (src:743-743)
GIVEN `a provision of the Act or the PPL rules requires the first person to satisfy the work test on a day for the purposes of a claim made by another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 33 applies to the first person as if they were the claimant` MEANS
    IF `a provision of the Act or the PPL rules requires the first person to satisfy the work test on a day for the purposes of a claim made by another person` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:778 | (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b), the PPL rules may prescribe what is, or is not, taken to be paid leave.
@ref s 34(2) (src:778-778)
GIVEN `the person takes a period of leave that is paid leave in the ordinary sense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the PPL rules prescribe whether the period is, or is not, taken to be paid leave` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a period of leave is paid leave` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the PPL rules prescribe whether the period is, or is not, taken to be paid leave`
    WHEN JUST prescribed THEN JUST prescribed
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST `the person takes a period of leave that is paid leave in the ordinary sense`

-- src:772 | (1) A person performs qualifying work on a day if at least one of the following applies on the day:
-- src:773 | (a) the person performs at least one hour of paid work;
-- src:774 | (b) the person takes a period of paid leave of at least one hour;
-- src:775 | (ca) the day is a flexible PPL day for a previous child of the person and parental leave pay was payable to the person on that day;
-- src:776 | (e) the day is in a jobkeeper payment period for the person;
-- src:777 | (f) the day is in a COVID-19 Australian Government payment period for the person.
@ref s 34(1) (src:772-777)
GIVEN d IS A `A day in the work test period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person performs qualifying work on a day` MEANS
       `at least one hour` (d's `hours of paid work performed`)
    OR `at least one hour` (d's `hours of paid leave taken`)
    OR (d's `a flexible PPL day for a previous child on which parental leave pay was payable`)
    OR (d's `in a jobkeeper payment period`)
    OR (d's `in a COVID-19 Australian Government payment period`)

-- src:779 | (3) A jobkeeper payment period for a person is a period for which:
-- src:780 | (a) an employer of the person is entitled to one or more jobkeeper payments for the person; or
-- src:781 | (b) the person themselves is entitled to one or more jobkeeper payments.
@ref s 34(3) (src:779-781)
GIVEN `an employer of the person is entitled to one or more jobkeeper payments for the person for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to one or more jobkeeper payments for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a period is a jobkeeper payment period for a person` MEANS
    JUST (`an employer of the person is entitled to one or more jobkeeper payments for the person for the period` OR `the person is entitled to one or more jobkeeper payments for the period`)

-- src:782 | (4) A jobkeeper payment is a payment that:
-- src:783 | (a) is payable by the Commonwealth in accordance with rules made under the Coronavirus Economic Response Package (Payments and Benefits) Act 2020; and
-- src:784 | (b) is known as jobkeeper payment.
@ref s 34(4) (src:782-784)
GIVEN `the payment is payable by the Commonwealth in accordance with rules made under the Coronavirus Economic Response Package (Payments and Benefits) Act 2020` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is known as jobkeeper payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a payment is a jobkeeper payment` MEANS
    JUST (`the payment is payable by the Commonwealth in accordance with rules made under the Coronavirus Economic Response Package (Payments and Benefits) Act 2020` AND `the payment is known as jobkeeper payment`)

-- src:785 | (5) A COVID-19 Australian Government payment period for a person is a period for which the person is entitled to a COVID-19 Australian Government payment.
@ref s 34(5) (src:785-785)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to a COVID-19 Australian Government payment for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a period is a COVID-19 Australian Government payment period for a person` MEANS
    JUST `the person is entitled to a COVID-19 Australian Government payment for the period`

-- src:786 | (6) A COVID-19 Australian Government payment is:
-- src:787 | (a) a payment or grant of financial assistance covered by item 492 of the table in Part 4 of Schedule 1AB to the Financial Framework (Supplementary Powers) Regulations 1997; or
-- src:788 | (b) a payment or grant of financial assistance by the Commonwealth that is prescribed by the PPL rules for the purposes of this paragraph.
@ref s 34(6) (src:786-788)
GIVEN `the payment or grant is covered by item 492 of the table in Part 4 of Schedule 1AB to the Financial Framework (Supplementary Powers) Regulations 1997` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment or grant is a payment or grant of financial assistance by the Commonwealth prescribed by the PPL rules for the purposes of paragraph 34(6)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a payment is a COVID-19 Australian Government payment` MEANS
    JUST (`the payment or grant is covered by item 492 of the table in Part 4 of Schedule 1AB to the Financial Framework (Supplementary Powers) Regulations 1997` OR `the payment or grant is a payment or grant of financial assistance by the Commonwealth prescribed by the PPL rules for the purposes of paragraph 34(6)(b)`)

-- src:791 | (1) A person performs paid work on a day if, on that day, the person performs work (whether as an employee, a contractor or otherwise and whether or not in Australia) for another entity for remuneration or other financial benefit.
-- src:792 | (2) However, a person is taken not to perform paid work for the purposes of subsection (1) if the other entity is controlled by the person (whether alone or with others).
-- src:793 | Self-employed
-- src:794 | (3) A person performs paid work on a day if, on that day, the person performs work for the purposes of a business that is carried on for profit (whether in or outside of Australia) by:
-- src:795 | (a) the person (whether alone or with others); or
-- src:796 | (b) an entity that is controlled by the person (whether alone or with others).
-- src:800 | (5) The PPL rules may prescribe what is, or is not, taken to be paid work.
@ref s 35(1)-(3) and (5) (src:791-800)
GIVEN `the person performs work for another entity for remuneration or other financial benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other entity is controlled by the person, alone or with others` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person performs work for the purposes of a business carried on for profit by the person or by an entity the person controls` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the PPL rules prescribe whether the work is, or is not, taken to be paid work` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person performs paid work on a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the PPL rules prescribe whether the work is, or is not, taken to be paid work`
    WHEN JUST prescribed THEN JUST prescribed
    WHEN NOTHING
        THEN JUST (       (`the person performs work for another entity for remuneration or other financial benefit` AND (NOT `the other entity is controlled by the person, alone or with others`))
                   OR `the person performs work for the purposes of a business carried on for profit by the person or by an entity the person controls`)

-- src:798 | (4) A person controls an entity if the person has the capacity to determine the outcome of decisions about the entity’s financial and operating policies.
@ref s 35(4) (src:798-798)
GIVEN `the person has the capacity to determine the outcome of decisions about the entity's financial and operating policies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person controls an entity` MEANS
    JUST `the person has the capacity to determine the outcome of decisions about the entity's financial and operating policies`

GIVEN hours IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the hours counted when a day has at least one hour of them and none otherwise` MEANS
    IF `at least one hour` hours THEN hours ELSE 0

-- src:803 | (1) For the purposes of step 5 of the method statement in section 32, if a person performs qualifying work on a day only because the day is a flexible PPL day for a previous child, the person is taken to have performed 7.6 hours of work on that day.
-- src:804 | If person performs paid work on previous flexible PPL day
-- src:805 | (2) For the purposes of step 5 of the method statement in section 32, if a person performs qualifying work on a day because both:
-- src:806 | (a) the person performs at least one hour of paid work on the day; and
-- src:807 | (b) the day is a flexible PPL day for which parental leave pay is payable to the person for a previous child;
-- src:808 | the person is taken to have performed on that day the greater of:
-- src:809 | (c) the hours of work the person would be taken to have performed if subsection (1) applied; and
-- src:810 | (d) the number of hours of paid work performed by the person on that day.
-- src:811 | If person takes paid leave on previous flexible PPL day
-- src:812 | (3) For the purposes of step 5 of the method statement in section 32, if a person performs qualifying work on a day because both:
-- src:813 | (a) the person takes a period of paid leave of at least one hour on the day; and
-- src:814 | (b) the day is a flexible PPL day for which parental leave pay is payable to the person for a previous child;
-- src:815 | the person is taken to have performed on that day the greater of:
-- src:816 | (c) the hours of work the person would be taken to have performed if subsection (1) applied; and
-- src:817 | (d) the number of hours of paid leave taken by the person on that day.
@ref s 35A (src:803-817)
GIVEN d IS A `A day in the work test period`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the hours of qualifying work on a day that is a flexible PPL day for a previous child` MEANS
    BRANCH IF work AND leave
           THEN (IF `the greater for subsection (2)` EQUALS `the greater for subsection (3)` THEN JUST `the greater for subsection (2)` ELSE NOTHING)
           IF work THEN JUST `the greater for subsection (2)`
           IF leave THEN JUST `the greater for subsection (3)`
           OTHERWISE JUST `the hours taken for a flexible PPL day for a previous child`
    WHERE
        work MEANS `at least one hour` (d's `hours of paid work performed`)
        leave MEANS `at least one hour` (d's `hours of paid leave taken`)
        `the greater for subsection (2)` MEANS maximum (LIST `the hours taken for a flexible PPL day for a previous child`, (d's `hours of paid work performed`))
        `the greater for subsection (3)` MEANS maximum (LIST `the hours taken for a flexible PPL day for a previous child`, (d's `hours of paid leave taken`))

-- src:819 | (1) For the purposes of step 5 of the method statement in section 32, if a person performs qualifying work on a day because the day is in a jobkeeper payment period for the person, the person is taken to have performed on that day the number of hours of work determined in accordance with the PPL rules.
-- src:820 | (2) Subsection (1) has effect:
-- src:821 | (a) even if the person also performs qualifying work on that day because of paragraph 34(1)(a), (b) or (ca); and
-- src:822 | (b) despite section 35A.
-- src:824 | (1) For the purposes of step 5 of the method statement in section 32, if a person performs qualifying work on a day because the day is in a COVID-19 Australian Government payment period for the person, the person is taken to have performed on that day the number of hours of work determined in accordance with the PPL rules.
-- src:825 | (2) Subsection (1) has effect:
-- src:826 | (a) even if the person also performs qualifying work on that day because of paragraph 34(1)(a), (b) or (ca); and
-- src:827 | (b) despite section 35A.
@ref s 35B and s 35C (src:819-827)
GIVEN d IS A `A day in the work test period`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the hours of qualifying work on a day in a jobkeeper payment period or a COVID-19 Australian Government payment period` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (d's `in a jobkeeper payment period`) AND (d's `in a COVID-19 Australian Government payment period`)
           THEN (IF (d's `hours taken for a jobkeeper payment period day under the PPL rules`) EQUALS (d's `hours taken for a COVID-19 Australian Government payment period day under the PPL rules`)
                 THEN JUST (d's `hours taken for a jobkeeper payment period day under the PPL rules`)
                 ELSE NOTHING)
           IF (d's `in a jobkeeper payment period`) THEN JUST (d's `hours taken for a jobkeeper payment period day under the PPL rules`)
           OTHERWISE JUST (d's `hours taken for a COVID-19 Australian Government payment period day under the PPL rules`)

GIVEN d IS A `A day in the work test period`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the hours of qualifying work a person is taken to have performed on a day` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (d's `in a jobkeeper payment period`) OR (d's `in a COVID-19 Australian Government payment period`)
           THEN `the hours of qualifying work on a day in a jobkeeper payment period or a COVID-19 Australian Government payment period` d
           IF (d's `a flexible PPL day for a previous child on which parental leave pay was payable`)
           THEN `the hours of qualifying work on a day that is a flexible PPL day for a previous child` d
           OTHERWISE JUST (`the hours counted when a day has at least one hour of them and none otherwise` (d's `hours of paid work performed`) PLUS `the hours counted when a day has at least one hour of them and none otherwise` (d's `hours of paid leave taken`))

-- src:829 | (1) A permissible break is any of the periods in subsections (2) and (3).
-- src:830 | Permissible break between 2 qualifying work days
-- src:831 | (2) If, between a day on which the person performed qualifying work (a qualifying work day) in the work test period and the next qualifying work day, there was at least 1 day but not more than 84 consecutive days on which the person did not perform qualifying work—the day or period of consecutive days between those 2 qualifying work days is a permissible break.
-- src:833 | (3) If:
-- src:834 | (a) a person performed qualifying work on a day (the earlier qualifying work day) before the first day in the work test period; and
-- src:835 | (b) the person next performed qualifying work on a day (the later qualifying work day) after the first day in the work test period; and
-- src:836 | (c) the later qualifying work day was no more than 84 consecutive days after the earlier qualifying work day;
-- src:837 | then the day or period of consecutive days on which the person did not perform qualifying work between the first day in the work test period and the later qualifying work day (including the first day of the work test period) is a permissible break.
@ref s 36(1)-(3) (src:829-837)
GIVEN k IS A NUMBER
      `the indexes of the qualifying work days` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the first day of the work test period` IS A DATE
      `the number of days in the work test period` IS A NUMBER
      `there is a qualifying work day before the first day of the work test period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days from that day to the first day of the work test period` IS A NUMBER
      `there is a qualifying work day after the last day of the work test period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days from the last day of the work test period to that day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the day at an index is a qualifying work day or falls within a permissible break` MEANS
    BRANCH IF elem k `the indexes of the qualifying work days` THEN TRUE
           IF hasEarlier AND hasLater
           THEN `the days between two qualifying work days are a permissible break` (nextIndex MINUS previousIndex MINUS 1)
           IF hasEarlier
           THEN (        `there is a qualifying work day after the last day of the work test period`
                 AND `the days between two qualifying work days are a permissible break`
                         (`the number of days in the work test period` PLUS `the number of days from the last day of the work test period to that day` MINUS previousIndex MINUS 2))
           IF hasLater
           THEN (        `there is a qualifying work day before the first day of the work test period`
                 AND `the later qualifying work day is no more than 84 days after the earlier`
                         (`the first day of the work test period` MINUS `the number of days from that day to the first day of the work test period`)
                         (`the first day of the work test period` PLUS nextIndex))
           OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        earlier MEANS filter (GIVEN j YIELD j LESS THAN k) `the indexes of the qualifying work days`
        later MEANS filter (GIVEN j YIELD j GREATER THAN k) `the indexes of the qualifying work days`
        hasEarlier MEANS NOT (null earlier)
        hasLater MEANS NOT (null later)
        previousIndex MEANS maximum earlier
        nextIndex MEANS minimum later

GIVEN hours IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the hours decided on a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER hours
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
    WHEN JUST x THEN x

GIVEN hours IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the hours are not decided on a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER hours
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST x THEN FALSE

-- src:728 | Step 4. Work out whether there is a period (a qualifying period) of 295 consecutive days in the work test period that are days:
-- src:729 | (a) on which the person has performed qualifying work; or
-- src:730 | (b) that fall within a permissible break.
-- src:731 | Step 5. If the person has performed at least 330 hours of qualifying work in a qualifying period, the person satisfies the work test.
@ref s 32, steps 4 and 5 of the method statement (src:728-731)
GIVEN `the covered flags` IS A LIST OF BOOLEAN
      `the decided hours of qualifying work on each day` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the days on which the hours are not decided` IS A LIST OF BOOLEAN
      start IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the window of 295 consecutive days from an index is a qualifying period with enough hours` MEANS
    IF NOT (and (take `the number of consecutive days in a qualifying period` (drop start `the covered flags`)))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF sumOfDecidedHours AT LEAST `the hours of qualifying work needed in a qualifying period`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF count (filter (GIVEN u YIELD u) (take `the number of consecutive days in a qualifying period` (drop start `the days on which the hours are not decided`))) GREATER THAN 0
              THEN NOTHING
              ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        sumOfDecidedHours MEANS sum (take `the number of consecutive days in a qualifying period` (drop start `the decided hours of qualifying work on each day`))

-- src:719 | 32 When a person satisfies the work test
-- src:720 | To work out whether a person satisfies the work test on a day, use the following method statement:
-- src:721 | Method statement
-- src:722 | Step 1. Work out the person’s work test period.
-- src:723 | Note: Work test period is defined in sections 33 and 33A for PPL claimants and special PPL claimants.
-- src:724 | Step 2. Work out the days in the work test period on which the person has and has not performed qualifying work.
-- src:725 | Note: Qualifying work is defined in section 34.
-- src:726 | Step 3. Work out whether any days on which the person has not performed qualifying work during the work test period fall within a permissible break.
-- src:727 | Note: Permissible break is defined in section 36.
-- src:728 | Step 4. Work out whether there is a period (a qualifying period) of 295 consecutive days in the work test period that are days:
-- src:729 | (a) on which the person has performed qualifying work; or
-- src:730 | (b) that fall within a permissible break.
-- src:731 | Step 5. If the person has performed at least 330 hours of qualifying work in a qualifying period, the person satisfies the work test.
@ref s 32 (src:719-731)
GIVEN `the claimant is a COVID-19 affected claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of the work test period` IS A DATE
      `there is a qualifying work day before the first day of the work test period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days from that day to the first day of the work test period` IS A NUMBER
      `there is a qualifying work day after the last day of the work test period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days from the last day of the work test period to that day` IS A NUMBER
      days IS A LIST OF `A day in the work test period`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person satisfies the work test by the method statement in section 32` MEANS
    IF NOT (n EQUALS (`the number of days in the work test period` `the claimant is a COVID-19 affected claimant`))
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE `some result in a list holds` (map (GIVEN start YIELD `the window of 295 consecutive days from an index is a qualifying period with enough hours` covered decided unclear start) (range 0 (n MINUS `the number of consecutive days in a qualifying period`)))
    WHERE
        n MEANS count days
        qualifyingFlags MEANS map (GIVEN d YIELD `a person performs qualifying work on a day` d) days
        qualifyingIndexes MEANS filter (GIVEN j YIELD at qualifyingFlags j) (range 0 (n MINUS 1))
        covered MEANS map (GIVEN k YIELD `the day at an index is a qualifying work day or falls within a permissible break` k qualifyingIndexes `the first day of the work test period` n `there is a qualifying work day before the first day of the work test period` `the number of days from that day to the first day of the work test period` `there is a qualifying work day after the last day of the work test period` `the number of days from the last day of the work test period to that day`) (range 0 (n MINUS 1))
        hoursByDay MEANS map (GIVEN d YIELD `the hours of qualifying work a person is taken to have performed on a day` d) days
        decided MEANS map `the hours decided on a day` hoursByDay
        unclear MEANS map `the hours are not decided on a day` hoursByDay

-- src:839 | (1) A person also satisfies the work test on a day if:
-- src:840 | (a) the Secretary is satisfied that either or both of the following circumstances existed:
-- src:841 | (i) if the person is covered by subsection (2)—the child was born prematurely;
-- src:842 | (ii) if the person is the child’s birth mother—while the person was pregnant with the child, the person had complications or illness related to the pregnancy which prevented the person from performing paid work; and
-- src:843 | (b) the Secretary is satisfied that the person would have satisfied the work test on the day in accordance with section 32 if that circumstance, or those circumstances, had not existed.
-- src:844 | (2) For the purposes of subparagraph (1)(a)(i), the following persons are covered:
-- src:845 | (a) the child’s birth mother;
-- src:846 | (b) a person who:
-- src:847 | (i) is a parent of the child; and
-- src:848 | (ii) is not the child’s birth mother;
-- src:849 | (c) the partner of the child’s birth mother.
@ref s 36A (src:839-849)
GIVEN `the person is the child's birth mother` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a parent of the child who is not the child's birth mother` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the partner of the child's birth mother` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary is satisfied that the child was born prematurely` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary is satisfied that, while the person was pregnant with the child, the person had complications or illness related to the pregnancy which prevented the person from performing paid work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary is satisfied that the person would have satisfied the work test on the day in accordance with section 32 if that circumstance, or those circumstances, had not existed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person also satisfies the work test on a day under section 36A` MEANS
    JUST (        (   (coveredBySubsection2 AND `the Secretary is satisfied that the child was born prematurely`)
                   OR (`the person is the child's birth mother` AND `the Secretary is satisfied that, while the person was pregnant with the child, the person had complications or illness related to the pregnancy which prevented the person from performing paid work`))
          AND `the Secretary is satisfied that the person would have satisfied the work test on the day in accordance with section 32 if that circumstance, or those circumstances, had not existed`)
    WHERE
        coveredBySubsection2 MEANS `the person is the child's birth mother` OR `the person is a parent of the child who is not the child's birth mother` OR `the person is the partner of the child's birth mother`

-- src:851 | A person also satisfies the work test on a day if:
-- src:852 | (a) the Secretary is satisfied that special circumstances of a kind prescribed by the PPL rules for the purposes of this paragraph exist in relation to the person on the day; and
-- src:853 | (b) the Secretary is satisfied that the person would have satisfied the work test on the day in accordance with section 32 if those circumstances had not existed.
@ref s 36AA (src:851-853)
GIVEN `the Secretary is satisfied that special circumstances of a kind prescribed by the PPL rules exist in relation to the person on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary is satisfied that the person would have satisfied the work test on the day in accordance with section 32 if those circumstances had not existed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person also satisfies the work test on a day under section 36AA` MEANS
    JUST (`the Secretary is satisfied that special circumstances of a kind prescribed by the PPL rules exist in relation to the person on the day` AND `the Secretary is satisfied that the person would have satisfied the work test on the day in accordance with section 32 if those circumstances had not existed`)

-- src:719 | 32 When a person satisfies the work test
-- src:720 | To work out whether a person satisfies the work test on a day, use the following method statement:
-- src:721 | Method statement
-- src:722 | Step 1. Work out the person’s work test period.
-- src:723 | Note: Work test period is defined in sections 33 and 33A for PPL claimants and special PPL claimants.
-- src:724 | Step 2. Work out the days in the work test period on which the person has and has not performed qualifying work.
-- src:725 | Note: Qualifying work is defined in section 34.
-- src:726 | Step 3. Work out whether any days on which the person has not performed qualifying work during the work test period fall within a permissible break.
-- src:727 | Note: Permissible break is defined in section 36.
-- src:728 | Step 4. Work out whether there is a period (a qualifying period) of 295 consecutive days in the work test period that are days:
-- src:729 | (a) on which the person has performed qualifying work; or
-- src:730 | (b) that fall within a permissible break.
-- src:731 | Step 5. If the person has performed at least 330 hours of qualifying work in a qualifying period, the person satisfies the work test.
-- src:839 | (1) A person also satisfies the work test on a day if:
-- src:840 | (a) the Secretary is satisfied that either or both of the following circumstances existed:
-- src:841 | (i) if the person is covered by subsection (2)—the child was born prematurely;
-- src:842 | (ii) if the person is the child’s birth mother—while the person was pregnant with the child, the person had complications or illness related to the pregnancy which prevented the person from performing paid work; and
-- src:843 | (b) the Secretary is satisfied that the person would have satisfied the work test on the day in accordance with section 32 if that circumstance, or those circumstances, had not existed.
-- src:851 | A person also satisfies the work test on a day if:
-- src:852 | (a) the Secretary is satisfied that special circumstances of a kind prescribed by the PPL rules for the purposes of this paragraph exist in relation to the person on the day; and
-- src:853 | (b) the Secretary is satisfied that the person would have satisfied the work test on the day in accordance with section 32 if those circumstances had not existed.
@ref s 32, s 36A, s 36AA (src:719-853)
GIVEN `the result of the method statement in section 32` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the result under section 36A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the result under section 36AA` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person satisfies the work test on a day` MEANS
    `some result in a list holds` (LIST `the result of the method statement in section 32`, `the result under section 36A`, `the result under section 36AA`)
